.TH SIA.CONF 5
.SH NAME
sia.conf, sia.key \- the assistant's settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/sia.conf
.br
.B /etc/sia.key
.SH DESCRIPTION
The assistant server,
.BR siad (4),
reads its settings from
.BR /etc/sia.conf ,
.IB key = value
lines, when it starts.
Root changes them with
.BI "sia config " KEY = VALUE
or the desktop's Settings (Assistant); siad then ends and
.BR init (8)
starts it again with them.
The API key of an online service is kept apart, in
.B /etc/sia.key
(mode 0600, root only), and added as one more
.B api_key=
line when read.
.TP
.B backend
.B local
(the default: the model on this computer) or
.B remote
(a service with an OpenAI-compatible API)
.TP
.B model
local: the model file (GGUF); none:
/models/smollm2-1.7b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf, or the first
.B .gguf
file in /models
.TP
.BR threads ", " ctx
local: how many threads compute; the context length in tokens (at least
256)
.TP
.BR url ", " api_model ", " api_key
remote: the server
.RB ( https://host/v1 ),
the model's name, the key
.TP
.B memory
.B on
(the default) or
.BR off :
nothing is saved, conversations live in memory only
.TP
.B compact_at
compact a conversation beyond this % of the model's context (default 60)
.TP
.B keep_turns
turns kept word for word after compaction (default 4)
.TP
.BR max_convs ", " max_log_kb
conversations kept per user (32); a log beyond this many KiB is compacted
(256)
.TP
.B remote_ctx
the context size assumed for a remote model (8192)
.TP
.B keep_loaded
1: the local model stays loaded when siad is idle (the default on machines
with 6 GiB or more)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
backend=remote
url=https://api.example.com/v1
api_model=some-model
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sia (1),
.BR siad (4)
